# Docker build context exclusions
#
# Without this file, `docker build` sends the ENTIRE working tree to the daemon
# — including bin/, obj/, runtime data/, log files, IDE caches. With a busy
# build agent, that often exceeds 1 GB and adds 10+ seconds per build before
# any layer cache check. Keeping this file lean costs nothing and makes
# rebuilds noticeably snappier.

# Build artifacts
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
publish/
artifacts/

# Runtime data — NEVER copy SQLite DB or logs into the image
**/data/
**/logs/
**/keys/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Test outputs
**/TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

# IDE / OS / VCS
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.pidb
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Docker meta (don't recurse)
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yaml

# Plans / scratch / docs
.claude/
*.local.md
LICENSE
README.md

# Secrets — defense in depth (real secrets should never be in repo, but if
# someone accidentally drops one, this stops it leaking into the image)
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
secrets/
.env
.env.*
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.local.json
